 it, why were you interested in the animal's claws? Because I was trying to see if it was a carnivore. How did you know that the animal is a mammal? Because it has hair. Why did you think it was a cheetah? Becaus", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=leXa7EKUPFk\u0026t=2364s", "end": 2414.89, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "503307685989d14d0980535d6ab77e7e60d6f1cdaf122598ddb1ac8dd2a8ad7d", "start": 2364.39, "text": "There's the MIT explanation. We know that temperature flow is equal to the fourth power of the temperature difference and the surface area and all that kind of stuff. We want to get them all together in a ball, sphere. The normal explanatio", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=leXa7EKUPFk\u0026t=2922s", "end": 2981.01, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "1c757271002e451f3bcdc9779b242b030d1f5e87201b0cf9f8f5c78a81f0584c", "start": 2922.27, "text": "But there's one thing that's well-illustrated by our particular capturing of Hamlet here. And that is that you'll note that the ratio of gray stuff to white stuff is considerable. The gray stuff is stuff that has been deduced by rules. And ", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}], "current_topic": "Playlist", "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpts": [{"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=leXa7EKUPFk\u0026t=400s", "end": 449.57, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "5f8cb2f8bc804b2acb177501e42a1af4edf71a399dc2bf1f6ebc0e527c547f8e", "start": 400.23, "text": "Have you ever written a program that's answered questions about its own behavior? Probably not. Would you like to learn how to do that? So by the end of the hour, you'll be able to write this program and many more like it that know how to a", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=leXa7EKUPFk\u0026t=808s", "end": 857.31, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id"