{"card_hash": "0f60855d02a485e128e62e2227970ee24a05b80651ff6fc7202d169a774ba93e", "channel": "Hustlers N The Hood", "chars": 19384, "chars_all_clips": 19384, "chars_chosen_clips": 1440, "clip_count": 14, "clips": [{"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=mL8umz2yvfQ\u0026t=59s", "end": 135.15, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "250e4a60baf820c4c5262e48c2b3512a33aa0b62ff3b3d5fdb7e76b468709c8a", "start": 59.605, "text": "compete. \u003e\u003e [music] \u003e\u003e Ain't no other record company out there that sold as many records as we did. We outsold Bad Boy, LaFace. Every black [singing and music] record label out there, we outsold them in one year. \u003e\u003e [music] \u003e\u003e All these wea", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=mL8umz2yvfQ\u0026t=191s", "end": 280.55, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "90c85cabe3a0cfadf36bb9a25be2fa50292d97e0f958323317fc7f49367564d7", "start": 191.8, "text": "\"Damn.\" \u003e\u003e That's [clears throat] what real competition does to your output. Not journaling about personal growth. Having actual faces [music] across from you. Names you refuse to lose to. People winning in territory you consider yours. And", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=mL8umz2yvfQ\u0026t=280s", "end": 364.51, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "c5899c6070fb40a4790f5232e2a4c86015c1d4ea214407667f507969e1c525d2", "start": 280.56, "text": "\u003e\u003e felt from my childhood. That's what makes me do what I do. \u003e\u003e Pain comes in, work comes out. By the time he had a record deal, that was the only way he knew how to operate. And here's where it gets really interesting, because what happen", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=mL8umz2yvfQ\u0026t=448s", "end": 553.471, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "0e30180ef35bad9fbae5936ddc0f29d203258a7e5628d94a0d2795d766e3b255", "start": 448.64, "text": "In 1986, a psychologist named James [music] Pennebaker tested this. He asked people to write about their worst experiences 15 minutes a day, 4 [music] days straight. The group that got it out visited the doctor at half the rate of those who", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=mL8umz2yvfQ\u0026t=677s", "end": 751.47, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "81e461a118996a41f0f3e8e8b36f3e1370bf4630d2ed4e410a65cf61540ffb28", "start": 677.76, "text": "them. \u003e\u003e And that sounds reckless. It sounds like a man who doesn't care about his craft. But listen to what the people around him [music] actually observed. His trumpet player Willie Waldman put it this way. \u003e\u003e Pac liked the flow. You That", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=mL8umz2yvfQ\u0026t=868s", "end": 960.6, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "683dd4f215a34a3df9a6df65ead4e53a1b76743f479bdfd927fc2402149bc9bf", "start": 868.68, "text": "\u003e\u003e My mother wrote a was in a book. There's [music] a book about my mother called \"Look For Me In The Worldwin\". I like to think that's my my motto. \u003e\u003e Look for me in the worldwin. And you can hear it in everything he did. At 15, he was pet", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}], "current_topic": "Job Hunt and Career", "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpts": [{"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=mL8umz2yvfQ\u0026t=59s", "end": 135.15, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "250e4a60baf820c4c5262e48c2b3512a33aa0b62ff3b3d5fdb7e76b468709c8a", "start": 59.605, "text": "compete. \u003e\u003e [music] \u003e\u003e Ain't no other record company out there that sold as many records as we did. We outsold Bad Boy, LaFace. Every black [singing and music] record label out there, we outsold them in one year. \u003e\u003e [music] \u003e\u003e All these wea", "timing": "source_